Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Prepend bos_before_voice.npy to the voice conditioning

Bundles from english_2026-04 on (bundle.json "insert_bos_before_voice":
true, "bos_before_voice_file": "bos_before_voice.npy") expect a BOS
embedding in front of the voice embedding when the voice conditions the
transformer. Without it the model produces noise instead of speech.

Load <models_dir>/bos_before_voice.npy once at construction when the
bundle has one (a small float32 .npy reader; older bundles have no such
file and are unchanged) and prepend it to each voice embedding when the
voice is first resolved. The on-disk .emb cache still holds the encoder
output alone.

voice_hash() now hashes the whole embedding: it hashed the first 16
floats, which with the BOS in front are the same for every voice, so a
second voice would have reused the first voice's KV snapshot.
